betterguac (1.6.0+bg10) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Activity page for administrators: sign-ins, failed sign-ins, sign-outs,
    two-factor events, server sessions with their length, admin changes and
    YAML sync applies, with filters, search, CSV export and 365-day
    retention.
  * Numbered database migrations, applied automatically on upgrade after a
    compressed backup of the database; betterguac-admin migrate [--status].
  * License: the Apache Guacamole WAR and its third-party libraries (EPL and
    CDDL among them) are shipped unmodified; betterguac-setup converts them
    from javax to jakarta on the installed machine with Debian's
    tomcat-jakartaee-migration (new dependency; betterguac-admin webapp
    rebuilds it). New /usr/share/doc/betterguac/SOURCES.
  * License: debian/copyright credits The Apache Software Foundation for the
    upstream files and Robert Debs for BetterGuac's own work.
  * License: change notices in every patched upstream file (guacd sources,
    index.html, the two MyBatis mapper files and the patched jar manifest).
  * Docker image: SBOM of every Debian package (TSV and SPDX 2.3) and a
    source notice in /usr/share/doc/betterguac/.
  * Tomcat RemoteIpValve: behind a reverse proxy on a private address, the
    Activity log and session history record the client's address from
    X-Forwarded-For; /etc/betterguac/trusted-proxies overrides the list.

 -- Robert Debs <robert@robertdebs.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:30:00 +0000

betterguac (1.6.0+bg9) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First account is a setup administrator: it signs in with the generated
    password and is not asked to enroll two-factor (TOTP attribute
    guac-totp-disabled=true). Its default password is a long random one.
  * YAML starter: the "delete []" note is on the connections and users lines.
  * README for release 1.6.0+bg9 is installed as
    /usr/share/doc/betterguac/README.md; README.Debian points to it.
  * betterguac-sync --help lists plan and apply, and explains the default
    /etc/betterguac/sync.env used by the betterguac-sync wrapper.

 -- Robert Debs <robert@robertdebs.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

betterguac (1.6.0+bg8) trixie; urgency=medium

  * One package for Debian 13 and Ubuntu 26.04: the JPEG library dependency
    now reads "libjpeg62-turbo (>= 1.3.1) | libjpeg62", since both provide
    libjpeg.so.62 with the LIBJPEG_6.2 symbols guacd uses (Debian names it
    libjpeg62-turbo, Ubuntu libjpeg62).
  * Depend on mariadb-server and mariadb-client directly instead of
    default-mysql-server, which is MySQL 8.4 on Ubuntu and broke setup.
    Installing BetterGuac on a machine that runs MySQL replaces it with
    MariaDB.

 -- Robert Debs <robert@robertdebs.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:15:00 +0000

betterguac (1.6.0+bg7) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Home page loading state: the stock grey spinning cog is replaced by a
    flat avocado silhouette with a steady double-beat pulse, centred on the
    midnight-blue background and gone exactly when the server list is ready.
  * The greeting row reserves its final size from first paint, so the server
    list no longer jumps down when the profile arrives.
  * The "BetterGuac is based on Apache Guacamole" credit is readable again:
    quiet grey, 11px, bottom right of the sign-in and home pages, and a
    separate thanks to Sesame for the AI tools used to build it. The Apache
    wording, links, NOTICE and license files are unchanged.
  * The avocado now shows from the very first paint: a small inline copy in
    index.html covers the wait while the page's scripts download on a slow
    link, then hands over to the home-page loader (or the sign-in page).
  * Release build: version 1.6.0+bg7 (was the test build 1.6.0+bg7~load1).

 -- Robert Debs <robert@robertdebs.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:10:45 +0000

